From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:11:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(entity-events): translate Bedrock actor events to Java
 statuses

Forward supported actor feedback through the current Java 26.3 status packet so taming, shaking, breeding, and other entity effects appear in the client. Preserve damage and death handling, add the missing non-player death effect, and cancel events without a translated output. Keep the mapping in a switch so unsupported Bedrock events remain explicit.

Preserve the upstream sparse ActorEvent wire IDs. Protocol documentation
renumbered omitted enum entries sequentially, but target BDS 1.26.51.1
build 51061372/protocol 2193 sends rocket explosion 25 and finished crossbow
charging 74. Matching native rocket code 143346100 also emits 25. Restore
the upstream IDs instead of applying the misleading documentation values.
Raw-ID translation tests cover the low and high sparse ranges, explosions,
totem feedback and charge completion. Raw evidence remains private.

Translate fishing bite event 13 into a capability-gated client message
bound to the hook's Java spawn UUID. The pinned native handler adds -0.5
using float arithmetic to the current local vertical motion. There is no
standard Java additive-motion packet for a tracked hook, and a core-side
velocity snapshot cannot preserve intervening client physics. Retain the
calculation and validation in core and use a minimal client callback.
Do not substitute a fixed velocity or assume a Java biting timer.

Bounded native execution verifies 108 impulse cases and 90 complete bite
handler cases against Windows 1.26.51.1 protocol 2193. Keep particles,
audio, subsequent physics, ordinary Java behavior and visible native
comparisons as separate remaining requirements.
